WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.331 --> 00:00:02.914
(gentle music)

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.110
- [Allison] The US is lifting
it's travel restrictions

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.610
for people who are entering
from foreign countries.

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.670
Starting November 8th,

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:14.680
as long as they are fully vaccinated

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.750
and can prove it,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.170
they can enter the US.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:20.500
This affects both air and
land border travelers.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.150
So here's what you need to
know about the new policy.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:27.122
(gentle music)

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:29.970
During the pandemic,

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.950
there were travel bans imposed
by the Trump Administration,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.040
and the new rules that
are going into effect

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.860
replace those banneds.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.340
Starting November 8th,

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.950
foreign nationals will be
allowed to enter the US

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.480
if they're fully vaccinated

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:44.360
and can show proof of vaccination.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.570
They also need to have
a negative COVID test

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.200
taken within three days

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.740
if they're traveling by air,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.370
but that negative COVID
test is not necessary

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.820
if they're traveling by land.

00:00:55.297 --> 00:00:57.880
(gentle music)

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.820
The acceptable vaccines

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.640
are ones that have been
authorized or approved

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.050
by the Food and Drug Administration,

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:09.550
or vaccines that have been
listed for emergency use

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.110
by the World Health Organization.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.440
So that includes the Pfizer vaccine,

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.953
Moderna, Johnson &amp; Johnson,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.770
as well as AstraZeneca and China's

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.030
Sinopharm and Sinovac vaccines.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.480
Russia's Sputnik V vaccine
has not been authorized

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.507
or approved by the FDA or WHO.

00:01:28.806 --> 00:01:31.389
(gentle music)

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.900
There are limited exemptions to the rules.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.110
So those include kids under 18,

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.610
certain vaccine clinical
trial participants,

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:41.460
and those with medical exemptions.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:42.760
There are exceptions for people

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.640
who need to travel for emergency
or humanitarian reasons,

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.080
but these people need to get

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.760
a US Government issued letter

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.400
that verifies their urgent need to travel.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.260
Now there are also exceptions for people

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.560
who are traveling on non-tourist visas

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.210
from countries with low
vaccine availability,

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:02.327
and those countries are
determined by the CDC.

00:02:02.327 --> 00:02:04.910
(gentle music)

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.490
There are also changes for US citizens

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.000
and lawful permanent residents

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.240
for returning from abroad by air.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:14.810
If you are fully vaccinated,

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.800
you'll need to show your
proof of vaccination

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.600
as well as a negative COVID test

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.800
that was taken within three days.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.490
But if you are unvaccinated,

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:24.520
you will need to show
a negative COVID test

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.433
that was taken within one day.

00:02:27.292 --> 00:02:29.875
(gentle music)

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.170
So kids who are under 18

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.900
are exempted from the
vaccination requirements.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.070
And this is because some younger kids

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.780
are currently ineligible for vaccination

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.900
and the vaccine availability for kids

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.430
varies across the globe.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.160
But kids between the ages of two and 17

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.780
do need to take a pre-departure COVID test

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.880
if they're flying,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.290
and that's regardless
of their citizenship.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.950
If they're traveling with
a fully vaccinated adults,

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.920
they can present a test that was taken

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.100
within three days of departure.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:01.490
But if they're traveling alone

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.430
or with unvaccinated adults,

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.750
then they need to present a test

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.313
that was taken within
one day of departure.

00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:10.896
(gentle music)

